$file — load a file from disk into the bundle

SUMMARY
  Reads a path given as the sole argument and appends one link to the
  appropriate array based on the file extension. Other input arrays are
  passed through unchanged.

SYNTAX
  $file('path/to/asset.mp3')
  $file(path='path/to/image.png')
  $file('_lang_desc', source_path=True)

INPUT
  prompts, texts, images, sounds, videos, files — unchanged (copied through)

OUTPUT
  Appends one new link to the array that matches the file extension:
    .mp3, .wav  → sounds[]
    .png, .jpg, .jpeg → images[]
    .mp4        → videos[]
    .txt        → texts[]
    other       → files[]

ARGUMENTS
  Positional string or path= / _path= — filesystem path to load.
  source_path=True — link to the original file (absolute path); no session copy.

BEHAVIOR
  Resolves the path relative to the current working directory, repo root,
  session directory, or sessions/** (for a bare filename). By default copies
  file bytes into a new link under the current op directory.

  With source_path=True, arrays hold an absolute path to the source file on
  disk (same as $folder(source_path=True)). Downstream externals read via
  ctx.read_link_text / read_link_bytes.

  AH_EMULATE_FILE=1 — write a placeholder link without reading disk (tests).

EXAMPLE
  @music: $file('music.mp3')
  @lang: $file('_lang_desc', source_path=True)

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No — prompts are not cleared after this call.
